@startuml
title Activiti 7 Guide Examples — Architecture Overview

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho

rectangle "Authenticated User" as AU
rectangle "Task API User\n(ROLE_ACTIVITI_USER)" as TU
rectangle "Human Participant" as HP
rectangle "Developer/Integrator" as DEV
rectangle "Cluster Operator" as OP

cloud "Keycloak\n(Identity Provider)" as KC
cloud "Public IP / External Access" as PUB

rectangle "Kubernetes / GKE Cluster" as K8s {
  component "NGINX Ingress Controller" as IN
  component "Example Runtime Bundle\n(Spring Boot + Spring Security)" as RB
  component "ProcessRuntime API" as PR
  component "TaskRuntime API" as TR
  component "Audit Service" as AUD
  component "Query Service" as QRY
  component "Notification Service" as NOTIF
  component "Cloud Connectors" as CC
  component "Deployment Descriptors\n+ Config Maps\n(input rate, replicas)" as DD
}

AU --> KC : Obtain token
TU --> KC : Obtain token

AU --> PUB : User endpoints (with token)
TU --> PUB : Task operations (with token)
DEV --> PUB : List definitions / Start SimpleProcess (with token)
OP --> IN : Configure routes\nand public IP

PUB --> IN : External requests
IN --> RB : Routed traffic

RB -down- PR
RB -down- TR

note right of TR
Requires logged-in user with
ACTIVITI_USER / ROLE_ACTIVITI_USER
end note

RB --> AUD : Emit/display audit events\nfor just-started instance
RB --> QRY : Expose process execution info

TU --> TR : TaskRuntime interaction
HP --> TR : Human task participation
DEV --> PR : ProcessRuntime interaction

note right of RB
Security, users, groups, and roles
via Spring Security in Spring Boot.
end note

DD -down-> RB : Configure replicas / input rate
DD -down-> QRY
DD -down-> AUD
DD -down-> NOTIF
DD -down-> CC

note bottom of K8s
Background components: Notification Service, Cloud Connectors.
They remain background unless requirements assign behavior.
end note

@enduml